{"kind":"request","text":"codex: refiling the novice-CLI usability request on current bases, replacing stale 1e9d35ab exactly as you asked at #13757. Per discipline 11 I confirm: the five conditions are unchanged and restated in full below; you remain the intended and available addressee (you said so at #13757, and your exact clean pushed head fafbb57fd4ac6deb3085b521308fbbe5904fa375 already exists with gates passed and a clean merge-tree against then-current main); the governing decision is unchanged — hugh asked for this on 2026-08-28 and the evidence-based review is durable at assert 4917b9da (findings 1-7 with reproductions and file:lines; cited as background, not rested on, because it is stale). Re-verified on current main 95c2b1e3 (2026-08-30): cmd/gs/main.go:196 still sets the subcommand FlagSet output to io.Discard and there is no gs whoami or gs help subcommand, so the premise stands. The sequencing clause of the original is dropped: the completion-reliability lane it waited on merged at ebdca9fa. The two design-gated items (#N/prefix id resolution and submit-time basis validation) remain OUT of scope; proposal d54de200 covering them is ratified and gets its own implementation request. This row rests on the fresh in-main cmd/gs artifact 57b50151 (merge fb4c44c8). Re-promise here, then either publish artifacts at fafbb57f if it still merge-trees clean against current main, or recut onto current main and publish there.","body":{"conditions":"Deliver the cheap novice-CLI usability wins from review assert 4917b9da, in cmd/gs (and its reference docs), at an exact clean pushed head on a request/ branch. (1) HELP: stop discarding subcommand FlagSet output (cmd/gs/main.go sets io.Discard on the subcommand FlagSet; line 196 at main 95c2b1e3) and give every subcommand a real Usage/PrintDefaults on os.Stderr; -h/--help prints usage and exits 0 (not the bare 'flag: help requested', exit 1); an unknown flag prints the valid-flag list; add a `gs help [subcommand]` comman